# Supabase Configuration
# The anon key is public by design (it is delivered to the browser); Row Level Security
# is the authorization boundary. Never put a service_role key in a VITE_ variable.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key

# Google Cloud Configuration (SERVER-SIDE ONLY)
# The Express backend authenticates with a Google service-account JSON file referenced by
# path (kept OUTSIDE git and gitignored), or via GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS.
# Never expose Google Cloud credentials to the browser, and never use a VITE_-prefixed
# variable for them: Vite inlines every VITE_ value into the shipped client bundle.
# See docs/security-remediation.md.

# Groq (SERVER-SIDE ONLY)
# Introduced by P3 of docs/python-migration-plan.md. Do NOT add VITE_GROQ_API_KEY --
# the previous VITE_ variable was inlined into the public client bundle and had to be
# rotated. Until P3 lands, the voice assistant uses its existing mock fallback.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
